   "Rotation NEVER changes which faces are adjacent to each other - only their apparent orientation/position changes",
   "Work through rotations incrementally (one 90-degree step at a time) rather than attempting a large rotation in one mental jump",
   "For a labelled/marked solid, track only the specific marking's new face+edge position after each rotation step, using the fixed-axis-cycle rule",
