   "For non-cube solids, adjacent faces in the net must share equal-length edges at the fold line, and folding must not cause any two faces to overlap",
   "The face that appears in the 'centre' of a cross-shaped cube net typically becomes the bottom (or front) face relative to the other four folding up around it",
